    {
      "explanation": "Emergency demand is elevated (growth~1.1) with node0 inventory low (9) and pipeline 44, node1 inventory 21 with no backlog, node2 inventory 62 with no backlog. HAPPO orders: node0=9, node1=15, node2=0. To avoid increasing downstream backlog and reduce total cost, we apply small coordinated corrections: (1) node0 raises order slightly to replenish pipeline and cover recent demand, but not excessively; (2) node1 trims order slightly because its inventory is ample and pipeline is 28, reducing upstream backlog risk; (3) node2 raises order modestly to build pipeline for future demand, but only if its inventory is low relative to recent demand; (4) default zero. All deltas are small and clipped.",
