      "explanation": "During a demand emergency, upstream nodes should not reduce orders based on low recent demand, as this starves downstream after pipeline delay. Node 0 (retail) should maintain or slightly increase orders to buffer against demand surges. Node 1 (regional) should increase orders to replenish its low inventory and cover backlog, while being mindful of its already high pipeline. Node 2 (supply) has ample inventory and should increase orders to support downstream replenishment. The rules use growth (recent/baseline) to detect demand drops and avoid over-reacting to temporary lulls. Corrections are small and coordinated to avoid creating excessive upstream backlog.",
